# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env
.go_private_token

# Build outputs
bin/
.coverage/
mockwf
# Root-anchored: a bare `server` (no leading slash) also matches the
# cmd/server/ *directory* at any depth, silently hiding real source files
# (wiring.go, wiring_test.go, exporters_test.go) from git. `/server` matches
# only a root-level `server` binary (e.g. from `go build ./cmd/server` run
# without -o from the repo root), which is what this was meant to ignore.
/server

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Claude Code agent worktrees (temporary, not project code)
.claude/worktrees/

# Temporary LLD extract (used by some scripts to feed the model)
.tmp-lld.md

# Staged PascalCase Glue schema copies (from make schema-register / CI)
.tmp/

# Local LLD reference — authoritative copy lives outside the repo at
# /Users/sharmila/bcbp-solutions/Documents/LLD/Org-Membership/Documents/
# The .claude/CLAUDE.md pointer references that external path.
iam-lld-org-membership-Final.md
